>> title: Passanda
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, indian, almond, cream, curry
>> counters: Curry House, One Pot
>> aka: pasanda, lamb passanda, chicken pasanda, pasande, shahi pasanda
>> pairs-with: pilau-rice, naan, ginger-garlic-paste
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> step.1: beat flat, marinate 2 hr
>> step.2: sweat 10 min, without colouring it
>> step.3: fry in 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 45 min, covered, on the lowest heat
>> step.5: stir in, simmer 5 min

Marinate @lamb leg steaks{2%lb}(900 g; beaten flat between sheets of plastic and cut in strips) with @thick yogurt{3/4%cup}(180 g), @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} ~marinate{2%hr}.

Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(finely chopped) in @ghee{4%Tbs}(56 g) in a #heavy pot{} under a lid ~fry{10%min}, keeping it pale.

Fry @ground almonds{1/2%cup}(50 g), @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @green cardamom{5%pods}(bruised) and @cinnamon{1%stick}(2-in piece) into @&(~1)softened onion{} ~fry{2%min}.

Simmer @&(~3)marinated lamb{} in @&(~1)almond masala{} with @water{1/2%cup}(120 mL), covered and on the lowest heat the ring will hold, ~simmer{45%min}. Yogurt sauces with no flour in them break at a boil and never come back.

Stir @heavy cream{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @garam masala{1/2%tsp} and @flaked almonds{2%Tbs}(toasted) into @&(~1)pot{} and ~simmer{5%min}.

Pasanda means the favourite piece, and the dish is defined by the cut and what is done to it: leg beaten flat so it cooks through in three-quarters of an hour and drinks up the yogurt. Alongside korma this is the other mild line, and the two are told apart by the almonds being ground and stirred in here rather than blended to a cream, and by the meat. Chicken pasanda exists; flattened breast, half the time.
